# An exported class is the route of its doors: building it and each public method, each called by the entry, the
# methods on the Store the building makes. What a call changes in place, it gives: `rows.append(Row(reading))` makes
# `rows` anew from the rows read and the Row built of the Reading, so the Reading reaches what is written at the place
# the store is made with, `Disk(Store.path)`. `get` builds the Readings back from the rows it reads: what goes in as a
# Reading comes out as one. The route reads the place and writes it again: it stands on both sides.

